+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered on `ToolRegistry` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` on `ToolDefinition` in `src/types/ai.ts` that is forwarded verbatim to the configured provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates incoming model arguments against that schema before the executor runs. A validation failure resolves to a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing, so a malformed call feeds back into the tool loop in `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` for the model to read and correct within the existing round budget instead of aborting the turn.
+
+## Validation in execute
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor, enforcing `required`, declared `type`, and `enum` constraints without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying defaults; invalid input returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing property path and constraint without calling the executor, while valid input (including unlisted extra properties) reaches the executor unchanged ([validated by: validates input against inputSchema in execute without invoking the executor or logging rejected values, while forwarding valid input unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L31)).
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` throws `Unknown tool: <name>` only when `name` is not registered; every schema validation failure on a registered tool resolves to a `ToolResponse` instead of rejecting.
+- Rejection messages and log lines emitted during validation report only the failing property paths and failed schema constraints, never the rejected property values themselves.
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- Registering a static `ToolDefinition` compiles its `inputSchema` during `register` and throws synchronously naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at register time when a static tool declares an uncompilable inputSchema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L93)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled once at registration and reused across repeated `execute` calls without recompiling.
+- Registering a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves the definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned on that call, caching compiled validators by schema identity so dynamic schemas never validate against a stale definition ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema returned on each call rather than a stale cached schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L108)).
+
+## Tool loop recovery
+
+- When the model emits a tool call that fails `inputSchema` validation, `createChatOrchestrator` forwards the rejection `ToolResponse.result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to supply corrected arguments on the next round and finish the turn without `processMessage` rejecting ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back through the orchestrator tool loop as a tool_result so the model can retry and resolve](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L152)).
